# Document history

A document's revision history lives in the `documentHistory` frontmatter — a
list of `{ version, date, description }` entries. Drop `\{% document-history /%}`
wherever the table should appear; the renderer builds it from the frontmatter,
so the data is authored once and every document's history table looks the same.

{% document-history /%}

The heading defaults to *Document history*. Pass `title=` to change it, or
`title=""` for the table on its own:

{% document-history title="Revision log" /%}
